config ZMK_LAYER_OVERLAY_REPORT
    bool "Report the active ZMK layer over the USB console for the layer-overlay companion app"
    default y
    depends on ZMK_USB_LOGGING
    help
      When enabled, prints a line like "ZMKLAYER:2" to the USB CDC-ACM
      console every time the active (highest) layer changes. Intended
      to be read by a host-side program that draws an on-screen overlay
      of the keymap.
